# project: gdpr-retention-cleanup
VAR chase_rounds = 0
VAR remediation_rounds = 0

-> data_inventory

=== data_inventory ===
Inventory personal data across all eleven teams: each team fills in the
data map. Done when every team has submitted a complete data map.
+ [All eleven data maps received] -> draft_schedule
+ [Some teams have not responded] -> chase_stragglers

=== chase_stragglers ===
Legal chases the teams that have not yet filled in their data map.
~ chase_rounds += 1
+ {chase_rounds < 6} [Chased — re-check responses] ~loop~ -> data_inventory
+ {chase_rounds >= 6} [Inventory stalled, human decides how to proceed] @human ~loop~ -> data_inventory

=== draft_schedule ===
Legal drafts the data-retention schedule from the completed inventory.
+ [Draft ready for DPO review] -> dpo_schedule_review

=== dpo_schedule_review ===
The DPO reviews the retention schedule and either approves it or bounces
it back to legal for redrafting, as often as needed.
+ [DPO approves the schedule] @human -> implement_deletion
+ [DPO bounces it for redrafting] @human ~loop~ -> draft_schedule

=== implement_deletion ===
Teams implement deletion jobs against the approved retention schedule.
Done when every team has deletion jobs ready for compliance review.
* [Deletion jobs implemented across teams] -> compliance_review

=== compliance_review ===
Per-team compliance review of the deletion jobs. Teams pass, fail for the
first time, or fail for a second time.
+ [All teams pass review] -> external_audit
+ [Some teams failed their first review] -> remediation
+ [A team has failed review twice] -> dpo_escalation

=== remediation ===
Failing teams (and any external-audit findings) get remediation tasks,
then go back for re-review.
~ remediation_rounds += 1
+ {remediation_rounds < 4} [Remediation done — re-review the teams] ~loop~ -> compliance_review
+ {remediation_rounds >= 4} [Remediation not converging] @human -> dpo_escalation

=== dpo_escalation ===
Teams that failed review twice go on the escalation list for the DPO,
who decides how to unblock them.
+ [DPO resolves the escalation — back to re-review] @human ~loop~ -> compliance_review

=== external_audit ===
External counsel performs the final audit once all teams have passed
compliance review.
+ [Audit clean, no findings] -> program_close
+ [Audit findings raised] ~loop~ -> remediation

=== program_close ===
The DPO formally closes the GDPR data-retention cleanup program.
* [DPO formally closes the program] @human -> file_report

=== file_report ===
Legal files the compliance report with the board.
* [Compliance report filed with the board] -> END
